     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times a day adds up to **5100 mg a day**. That's twice the maximum labeled dose of immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day) and well above the extended-release maximum (2000 mg/day). At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and severe stomach side effects goes up a lot.\n\nThis looks like it may be a mix-up between a total daily dose and a per-dose amount. The usual regimens near this number are:\n\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n2. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth, twice daily with meals** (1700 mg/day total)\n3. **Metformin 1000 mg by mouth, twice daily with meals** (2000 mg/day)\n\nShould I enter one of these, or a different dose? If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that the over-maximum dose was intentional. That would normally also go to pharmacy for review."
      }
     ],
